{%- comment -%}
  ow-money — prints one price the way the rest of Be Yours does: with the
  currency code ("$24.00 AUD") when Theme settings > Currency format > "Show
  currency codes" (settings.currency_code_enabled) is on, without it ("$24.00")
  when off. Same rule as the vendor's snippets/price.liquid.

  Every custom section prints prices through this, so the merchant's one
  setting decides the format site-wide. assets/ow-money.js is the JS twin
  that re-renders prices after a variant/plan change — keep the two in step.

  Accepts:
  - amount: {Number} price in cents

  Usage:
  {% render 'ow-money', amount: product.price %}
  To use the result inside other text, capture it first:
  {%- capture price_str -%}{% render 'ow-money', amount: product.price %}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if settings.currency_code_enabled -%}{{ amount | money_with_currency }}{%- else -%}{{ amount | money }}{%- endif -%}
